IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulations 16, 16A and 17: the risk assessments made by the Treasury and the Home Office, by the Treasury alone (proliferation
-- financing) and by each supervisory authority.  These are duties of public bodies, not of a relevant person; the seat reads them as the
-- sources of the information a relevant person must take into account under regulations 18 and 18A.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- HOW A DUTY READS HERE.  A duty function answers whether the requirement is met on the facts stated: JUST TRUE when every condition
-- holds; JUST FALSE when one does not (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no); JUST TRUE also when a
-- "where" or "if" that triggers the requirement is not reached, because no requirement has then arisen to be unmet (ruling 2026-11-05,
-- (b); fork F-where in NOTES.md).  What "appropriate" or "as soon as reasonably practicable" requires is a judgement
-- the text leaves to whoever applies it: it arrives as a BOOLEAN input.

§ `Regulation 16 -- Risk assessment by the Treasury and Home Office`

-- reg 16(1).  The Treasury and the Home Office must make arrangements before 26th June 2018 for a risk assessment to be undertaken to
-- identify, assess, understand and mitigate the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing affecting the United Kingdom.
-- src:408 | (1) The Treasury and the Home Office must make arrangements before 26th June 2018 for a risk assessment to be undertaken to identify, assess, understand and mitigate the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing affecting the United Kingdom (“the risk assessment”).
@ref reg 16(1) (src:408-408)
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 16(1) the date before which the arrangements must be made` MEANS Date 26 6 2018

@ref reg 16(1) (src:408-408)
GIVEN `the date on which the Treasury and the Home Office made arrangements for a risk assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1) the Treasury and the Home Office made the arrangements in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the Treasury and the Home Office made arrangements for a risk assessment`) MINUS (Day `reg 16(1) the date before which the arrangements must be made`) AT MOST -1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must make arrangements before 26th June 2018" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 16(1), who bears the duty.  The text names the bearer: "The Treasury and the Home Office must make arrangements".
@ref reg 16(1) (src:408-408)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 16(1) the bearer of the duty to make the arrangements` MEANS "the Treasury and the Home Office"

-- reg 16(2).  The risk assessment must, among other things, do four things.  "Among other things" leaves the list open, so the function
-- answers only whether these four are done.
-- src:409 | (2) The risk assessment must, among other things—
-- src:410 | (a) identify any areas where relevant persons should apply enhanced customer due diligence measures, and where appropriate, specify the measures to be taken;
-- src:411 | (b) identify, where appropriate, the sectors or areas of lower and greater risk of money laundering and terrorist financing;
-- src:412 | (c) consider whether any rules on money laundering and terrorist financing made by a supervisory authority applying in relation to the sector it supervises are appropriate in the light of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing applying to that sector;
-- src:413 | (d) provide the information and analysis necessary to enable it to be used for the purposes set out in paragraph (3).
@ref reg 16(2) (src:409-413)
GIVEN `it identifies any areas where relevant persons should apply enhanced customer due diligence measures and, where appropriate, specifies the measures to be taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies, where appropriate, the sectors or areas of lower and greater risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considers whether any rules made by a supervisory authority for the sector it supervises are appropriate in the light of the risks applying to that sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides the information and analysis necessary for the purposes set out in paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16(2) the risk assessment does what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it identifies any areas where relevant persons should apply enhanced customer due diligence measures and, where appropriate, specifies the measures to be taken` AND `it identifies, where appropriate, the sectors or areas of lower and greater risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` AND `it considers whether any rules made by a supervisory authority for the sector it supervises are appropriate in the light of the risks applying to that sector` AND `it provides the information and analysis necessary for the purposes set out in paragraph (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The risk assessment must, among other things—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 16(3).  The Treasury and the Home Office must ensure that the risk assessment is used to do three things.
