      `the risk assessment is used to consider whether the exclusions provided for in regulation 15 are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk assessment is used to consider whether providers of gambling services other than casinos should continue to be excluded from the requirements of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16(3) the Treasury and the Home Office ensure that the risk assessment is used as paragraph (3) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the risk assessment is used to consider the appropriate allocation and prioritisation of resources to counter money laundering and terrorist financing` AND `the risk assessment is used to consider whether the exclusions provided for in regulation 15 are being abused` AND `the risk assessment is used to consider whether providers of gambling services other than casinos should continue to be excluded from the requirements of these Regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Treasury and the Home Office must ensure that the risk assessment is used to—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

