        IF `the joint report sets out, as appropriate, the findings of the risk assessment` AND `it was prepared as soon as reasonably practicable after the risk assessment was completed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Treasury and the Home Office must prepare a joint report setting out, as appropriate, the findings of the risk assessment as soon as reasonably practicable" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

