-- reg 16(8).  If information from the risk assessment would assist the supervisory authorities in carrying out their own risk
-- assessment, the Treasury and the Home Office must, where appropriate, make that information available to them, unless to do so would
-- not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018 or any other enactment, or the UK GDPR.
-- src:430 | (8) If information from the risk assessment would assist the supervisory authorities in carrying out their own money laundering and terrorist financing risk assessment, the Treasury and the Home Office must, where appropriate, make that information available to those supervisory authorities, unless to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under —
-- src:431 | (a) the Data Protection Act 2018 or any other enactment, or
-- src:432 | (b) the UK GDPR.
@ref reg 16(8) (src:430-432)
GIVEN `the information is made available to the supervisory authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018, any other enactment or the UK GDPR` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information from the risk assessment would assist the supervisory authorities in carrying out their own money laundering and terrorist financing risk assessment, and it is appropriate to make it available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16(8) the Treasury and the Home Office make information from the risk assessment available to the supervisory authorities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`information from the risk assessment would assist the supervisory authorities in carrying out their own money laundering and terrorist financing risk assessment, and it is appropriate to make it available`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "information from the risk assessment would assist the supervisory authorities in carrying out their own money laundering and terrorist financing risk assessment, and it is appropriate to make it available" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018, any other enactment or the UK GDPR` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018, any other enactment or the UK GDPR"
        IF `the information is made available to the supervisory authorities` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Treasury and the Home Office must, where appropriate, make that information available to those supervisory authorities" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

