-- reg 16A(9).  "Proliferation financing" means the act of providing funds or financial services for use, in whole or in part, in the
-- manufacture, acquisition, development, export, trans-shipment, brokering, transport, transfer, stockpiling of, or otherwise in
-- connection with the possession or use of, chemical, biological, radiological or nuclear weapons (including the means of delivery of such
-- weapons and other CBRN-related goods and technology), in contravention of a relevant financial sanctions obligation.
-- src:447 | (9) In this regulation, “proliferation financing” means the act of providing funds or financial services for use, in whole or in part, in the manufacture, acquisition, development, export, trans-shipment, brokering, transport, transfer, stockpiling of, or otherwise in connection with the possession or use of, chemical, biological, radiological or nuclear weapons, including the provision of funds or financial services in connection with the means of delivery of such weapons and other CBRN-related goods and technology, in contravention of a relevant financial sanctions obligation.
@ref reg 16A(9) (src:447-447)
GIVEN `the act is providing funds or financial services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the funds or services are for use, in whole or in part, in connection with chemical, biological, radiological or nuclear weapons, their means of delivery or other CBRN-related goods and technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is in contravention of a relevant financial sanctions obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(9) the act is proliferation financing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is providing funds or financial services` AND `the funds or services are for use, in whole or in part, in connection with chemical, biological, radiological or nuclear weapons, their means of delivery or other CBRN-related goods and technology` AND `the act is in contravention of a relevant financial sanctions obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“proliferation financing” means the act of providing funds or financial services for use ... in contravention of a relevant financial sanctions obligation"

-- reg 16A(10).  Definitions for the regulation.  Each defined term has its own answer.
-- "biological weapon" means a biological agent or toxin (within the meaning of section 1(1)(a) of the Biological Weapons Act 1974) in a
-- form capable of use for hostile purposes, or anything to which section 1(1)(b) of that Act applies.
-- src:448 | (10) In this regulation—
-- src:449 | “biological weapon” means a biological agent or toxin (within the meaning of section 1(1)(a) of the Biological Weapons Act 1974) in a form capable of use for hostile purposes or anything to which section 1(1)(b) of that Act applies;
@ref reg 16A(10) “biological weapon” (src:448-449)
GIVEN `it is a biological agent or toxin within the meaning of section 1(1)(a) of the Biological Weapons Act 1974 in a form capable of use for hostile purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is anything to which section 1(1)(b) of that Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is a biological weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a biological agent or toxin within the meaning of section 1(1)(a) of the Biological Weapons Act 1974 in a form capable of use for hostile purposes` OR `it is anything to which section 1(1)(b) of that Act applies` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“biological weapon” means a biological agent or toxin ... or anything to which section 1(1)(b) of that Act applies"

-- "chemical weapon" has the meaning given by section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996: a pointer outside the text.
-- src:450 | “chemical weapon” has the meaning given by section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996;
@ref reg 16A(10) “chemical weapon” (src:450-450)
GIVEN `section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996 answers that the thing is a chemical weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is a chemical weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996 answers that the thing is a chemical weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996 answers that the thing is a chemical weapon` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“chemical weapon” has the meaning given by section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996" (the Act answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by section 1 of the Chemical Weapons Act 1996

-- "CBRN-related goods and technology" means technology (including dual-use technology) and dual-use goods used for non-legitimate
-- purposes in connection with the matters referred to in paragraph (9).
-- src:451 | “CBRN-related goods and technology” means technology (including dual-use technology) and dual-use goods used for non-legitimate purposes in connection with the matters referred to in paragraph (9);
@ref reg 16A(10) “CBRN-related goods and technology” (src:451-451)
GIVEN `it is technology, including dual-use technology, or dual-use goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used for non-legitimate purposes in connection with the matters referred to in paragraph (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is CBRN-related goods and technology` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is technology, including dual-use technology, or dual-use goods` AND `it is used for non-legitimate purposes in connection with the matters referred to in paragraph (9)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“CBRN-related goods and technology” means technology (including dual-use technology) and dual-use goods used for non-legitimate purposes"

-- "dual-use goods" means (a) any thing for the time being specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation, other than any thing which is
-- dual-use technology, and (b) any tangible storage medium on which dual use technology is recorded or from which it can be derived.
-- src:452 | “dual-use goods” means (a) any thing for the time being specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation, other than any thing which is dual-use technology, and (b) any tangible storage medium on which dual use technology is recorded or from which it can be derived;
