GIVEN `it is specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is dual-use technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a tangible storage medium on which dual use technology is recorded or from which it can be derived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is dual-use goods` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`it is specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation` AND (NOT (`it is dual-use technology`))) OR `it is a tangible storage medium on which dual use technology is recorded or from which it can be derived` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“dual-use goods” means (a) any thing ... specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation, other than any thing which is dual-use technology, and (b) any tangible storage medium"

-- "Dual-Use Regulation" means Council Regulation (EC) No 428/2009 of 5 May 2009 (a name).
-- src:453 | “Dual-Use Regulation” means Council Regulation (EC) No 428/2009 of 5 May 2009 setting up a Community regime for the control of exports, transfer, brokering and transit of dual-use items;
@ref reg 16A(10) “Dual-Use Regulation” (src:453-453)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 16A(10) “Dual-Use Regulation” means` MEANS
    "Council Regulation (EC) No 428/2009 of 5 May 2009 setting up a Community regime for the control of exports, transfer, brokering and transit of dual-use items"

-- "dual-use technology" means any thing for the time being specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation which is described as
-- software or technology.
-- src:454 | “dual-use technology” means any thing for the time being specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation which is described as software or technology;
@ref reg 16A(10) “dual-use technology” (src:454-454)
GIVEN `it is specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is described there as software or technology` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is dual-use technology` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation` AND `it is described there as software or technology` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“dual-use technology” means any thing for the time being specified in Annex I of the Dual-Use Regulation which is described as software or technology"

-- "nuclear weapon" includes a nuclear explosive device that is not intended for use as a weapon.  A list that "includes": not closed.
-- src:455 | “nuclear weapon” includes a nuclear explosive device that is not intended for use as a weapon;
@ref reg 16A(10) “nuclear weapon” (src:455-455)
GIVEN `it is a nuclear explosive device that is not intended for use as a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is a nuclear weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a nuclear explosive device that is not intended for use as a weapon` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“nuclear weapon” includes a nuclear explosive device that is not intended for use as a weapon"

-- "radiological weapon" means a device designed to cause destruction, damage or injury by means of the radiation produced by the decay of
-- radioactive material.
-- src:456 | “radiological weapon” means a device designed to cause destruction, damage or injury by means of the radiation produced by the decay of radioactive material;
@ref reg 16A(10) “radiological weapon” (src:456-456)
GIVEN `it is a device designed to cause destruction, damage or injury by means of the radiation produced by the decay of radioactive material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is a radiological weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a device designed to cause destruction, damage or injury by means of the radiation produced by the decay of radioactive material` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“radiological weapon” means a device designed to cause destruction, damage or injury by means of the radiation produced by the decay of radioactive material"

-- "relevant financial sanctions obligation" means a prohibition or requirement in regulations made under section 1 of the Sanctions and
-- Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 and imposed for one or more of the purposes in section 3(1) or (2) of that Act so far as it relates to
-- compliance with a relevant UN obligation.
-- src:457 | “relevant financial sanctions obligation” means a prohibition or requirement in regulations made under section 1 of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 and imposed for one or more of the purposes in section 3(1) or (2) of that Act so far as it relates to compliance with a relevant UN obligation;
@ref reg 16A(10) “relevant financial sanctions obligation” (src:457-457)
GIVEN `it is a prohibition or requirement in regulations made under section 1 of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is imposed for one or more of the purposes in section 3(1) or (2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to compliance with a relevant UN obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the obligation is a relevant financial sanctions obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a prohibition or requirement in regulations made under section 1 of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018` AND `it is imposed for one or more of the purposes in section 3(1) or (2) of that Act` AND `it relates to compliance with a relevant UN obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant financial sanctions obligation” means a prohibition or requirement in regulations made under section 1 of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 ..."

-- "relevant UN obligation" means an obligation that the UK has by virtue of a resolution adopted by the Security Council of the United
-- Nations which relates to the prevention, suppression and disruption of the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction and the financing of such.
-- src:458 | “relevant UN obligation” means an obligation that the UK has by virtue of a resolution adopted by the Security Council of the United Nations which relates to the prevention, suppression and disruption of the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction and the financing of such;
@ref reg 16A(10) “relevant UN obligation” (src:458-458)
GIVEN `it is an obligation that the UK has by virtue of a resolution adopted by the Security Council of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution relates to the prevention, suppression and disruption of the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction and the financing of such` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the obligation is a relevant UN obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an obligation that the UK has by virtue of a resolution adopted by the Security Council of the United Nations` AND `the resolution relates to the prevention, suppression and disruption of the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction and the financing of such` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant UN obligation” means an obligation that the UK has by virtue of a resolution adopted by the Security Council of the United Nations which relates to the prevention, suppression and disruption of the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction"

-- "technology" has the meaning given by paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018: a pointer outside the text.
-- src:459 | “technology” has the meaning given by paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018.
@ref reg 16A(10) “technology” (src:459-459)
GIVEN `paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 answers that the thing is technology` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16A(10) the thing is technology` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 answers that the thing is technology` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 answers that the thing is technology` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“technology” has the meaning given by paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018" (the Act answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by paragraph 37 of Schedule 1 to the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018

§ `Regulation 17 -- Risk assessment by supervisory authorities`

-- reg 17(1).  Each supervisory authority must identify and assess the international and domestic risks of money laundering and terrorist
-- financing to which those relevant persons for which it is the supervisory authority ("its own sector") are subject.
-- src:461 | (1) Each supervisory authority must identify and assess the international and domestic risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which those relevant persons for which it is the supervisory authority (“its own sector”) are subject.
@ref reg 17(1) (src:461-461)
GIVEN `it identifies and assesses the international risks to which the relevant persons in its own sector are subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies and assesses the domestic risks to which the relevant persons in its own sector are subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(1) the supervisory authority identifies and assesses the risks to its own sector` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it identifies and assesses the international risks to which the relevant persons in its own sector are subject` AND `it identifies and assesses the domestic risks to which the relevant persons in its own sector are subject` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each supervisory authority must identify and assess the international and domestic risks of money laundering and terrorist financing" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(1), who bears the duty.  The text names the bearer: "Each supervisory authority must identify and assess".
@ref reg 17(1) (src:461-461)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 17(1) the bearer of the duty to identify and assess the risks` MEANS "each supervisory authority, as to the relevant persons in its own sector"

-- reg 17(2).  In carrying out the risk assessment the authority must take into account the Treasury and Home Office report under regulation
-- 16(6) and the information made available under regulation 16(8).  (Paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) are shown blank in this text.)
-- src:462 | (2) In carrying out the risk assessment required under paragraph (1), the supervisory authority must take into account—
-- src:463 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:464 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:465 | (c) the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(6); and
-- src:466 | (d) information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(8).
@ref reg 17(2) (src:462-466)
GIVEN `it takes into account the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it takes into account the information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(2) the supervisory authority takes into account what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it takes into account the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(6)` AND `it takes into account the information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the supervisory authority must take into account—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(3).  A supervisory authority must keep an up-to-date record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1).
-- src:467 | (3) A supervisory authority must keep an up-to-date record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1).
@ref reg 17(3) (src:467-467)
GIVEN `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(3) the supervisory authority keeps the record paragraph (3) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` AND `the record is up to date` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep an up-to-date record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(4).  Each supervisory authority must develop and record in writing risk profiles for each relevant person in its own sector.
-- src:468 | (4) Each supervisory authority must develop and record in writing risk profiles for each relevant person in its own sector.
@ref reg 17(4) (src:468-468)
GIVEN `it develops risk profiles for each relevant person in its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it records the risk profiles in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(4) the supervisory authority develops and records the risk profiles` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it develops risk profiles for each relevant person in its own sector` AND `it records the risk profiles in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must develop and record in writing risk profiles for each relevant person in its own sector" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(5).  A supervisory authority may prepare a single risk profile in relation to two or more relevant persons in its sector, if
-- (a) the relevant persons share similar characteristics; and (b) the risks affecting them do not differ significantly.
-- src:469 | (5) A supervisory authority may prepare a single risk profile under paragraph (4) in relation to two or more relevant persons in its sector, if—
-- src:470 | (a) the relevant persons share similar characteristics; and
-- src:471 | (b) the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing affecting those relevant persons do not differ significantly.
@ref reg 17(5) (src:469-471)
GIVEN `the relevant persons share similar characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing affecting those relevant persons do not differ significantly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(5) the supervisory authority may prepare a single risk profile` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant persons share similar characteristics` AND `the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing affecting those relevant persons do not differ significantly` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may prepare a single risk profile ... if, (a) the relevant persons share similar characteristics; and (b) the risks ... do not differ significantly" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 17(6).  Where an authority has prepared a single risk profile for a cluster, it must keep under review whether an individual risk
-- profile should be prepared for any relevant person in the cluster because (5)(a) or (b) (or both) are no longer satisfied in relation to that person.
-- src:472 | (6) Where a supervisory authority has prepared a single risk profile for two or more relevant persons in its sector (a “cluster”), the supervisory authority must keep under review whether an individual risk profile should be prepared in relation to any relevant person in the cluster because sub-paragraph (a) or (b) (or both sub-paragraphs) of paragraph (5) are no longer satisfied in relation to that person.
@ref reg 17(6) (src:472-472)
GIVEN `it keeps under review whether an individual risk profile should be prepared for any relevant person in the cluster` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has prepared a single risk profile for two or more relevant persons in its sector (a cluster)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(6) the supervisory authority keeps the cluster under review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the supervisory authority has prepared a single risk profile for two or more relevant persons in its sector (a cluster)`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the supervisory authority has prepared a single risk profile for two or more relevant persons in its sector (a cluster)" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it keeps under review whether an individual risk profile should be prepared for any relevant person in the cluster` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the supervisory authority must keep under review whether an individual risk profile should be prepared" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(7).  In developing the risk profiles the authority must take full account of the risks that relevant persons in its own sector
-- will not take appropriate action to identify, understand and mitigate the risks.
-- src:473 | (7) In developing the risk profiles referred to in paragraph (4), the supervisory authority must take full account of the risks that relevant persons in its own sector will not take appropriate action to identify, understand and mitigate money laundering and terrorist financing risks.
@ref reg 17(7) (src:473-473)
GIVEN `it takes full account of the risks that relevant persons in its own sector will not take appropriate action to identify, understand and mitigate money laundering and terrorist financing risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(7) the supervisory authority takes full account of the risk of inaction in its sector` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it takes full account of the risks that relevant persons in its own sector will not take appropriate action to identify, understand and mitigate money laundering and terrorist financing risks` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take full account of the risks that relevant persons in its own sector will not take appropriate action" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(8).  Each authority must review the risk profiles at regular intervals and following any significant event or developments which
-- might affect the risks to which its own sector is subject, such as (a) to (e).  "Such as" leaves the list of events open.
-- src:474 | (8) Each supervisory authority must review the risk profiles developed under paragraph (4) at regular intervals and following any significant event or developments which might affect the risks to which its own sector is subject, such as—
-- src:475 | (a) significant external events that change the nature of the money laundering or terrorist financing risks;
-- src:476 | (b) emerging money laundering or terrorist financing risks;
-- src:477 | (c) any findings resulting from measures taken by other supervisory authorities;
-- src:478 | (d) any changes in the way in which its own sector is operated;
-- src:479 | (e) significant changes in regulation.
@ref reg 17(8) (src:474-479)
GIVEN `it reviews the risk profiles at regular intervals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it reviews the risk profiles following any significant event or developments which might affect the risks to which its own sector is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(8) the supervisory authority reviews the risk profiles` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it reviews the risk profiles at regular intervals` AND `it reviews the risk profiles following any significant event or developments which might affect the risks to which its own sector is subject` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each supervisory authority must review the risk profiles developed under paragraph (4) at regular intervals and following any significant event or developments" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 17(9).  If information from the risk assessment, or provided under regulation 16(8), would assist relevant persons in carrying out their
-- own risk assessment, the authority must, where appropriate, make it available to them, unless to do so would not be compatible with
-- restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018 or any other enactment, or the UK GDPR.
-- SEAM S-2 (answering): regulation 18(2)(a) takes the fact that this information was made available.
-- src:480 | (9) If information from the risk assessment carried out under paragraph (1), or from information provided to the supervisory authority under regulation 16(8), would assist relevant persons in carrying out their own money laundering and terrorist financing risk assessment, the supervisory authority must, where appropriate, make that information available to those persons, unless to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under —
-- src:481 | (a) the Data Protection Act 2018 or any other enactment, or
-- src:482 | (b) the UK GDPR.
@ref reg 17(9) (src:480-482)
GIVEN `the information is made available to the relevant persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018, any other enactment or the UK GDPR` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information from the risk assessment, or provided under regulation 16(8), would assist relevant persons in carrying out their own risk assessment, and it is appropriate to make it available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 17(9) the supervisory authority makes information available to the relevant persons in its sector` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`information from the risk assessment, or provided under regulation 16(8), would assist relevant persons in carrying out their own risk assessment, and it is appropriate to make it available`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "information from the risk assessment, or provided under regulation 16(8), would assist relevant persons in carrying out their own risk assessment, and it is appropriate to make it available" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018, any other enactment or the UK GDPR` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "to do so would not be compatible with restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under the Data Protection Act 2018, any other enactment or the UK GDPR"
        IF `the information is made available to the relevant persons` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the supervisory authority must, where appropriate, make that information available to those persons" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)
